# Biz Intel vs ATO Annual / Company CTR

## Two different bugs (do not conflate)

| Issue | Symptom | Cause |
|-------|---------|--------|
| **Cash universe drop** | Annual expenses ~$13,012 vs Biz Intel ~$15,346 (gap **$2,334.20** = one Stamp zone) | OCR/Manual collapse on bank+cash feed |
| **GST basis** | Biz Intel cash Net **−$927** vs tax Net **~−$1,674** | Inclusive cash vs ex-GST (`total*ExGst`) |

ATO Lodgment Annual / CTR are **for OSB / myTax entry** → primary figures must be **GST-exclusive (tax)**.  
Biz Intel keeps **cash (GST-incl.)** as the large P&L figure, with tax beside it.

## Confirmed SELPIC FY 2025–26 (same ledger)

| Screen | Basis | Income | Expenses | Net |
|--------|-------|--------|----------|-----|
| **Biz Intel** | Cash (incl.) | ~$14,419.48 | ~$15,346.61 | **−$927.13** |
| **Biz Intel** | Tax (ex GST est.) | cash − 1A | cash − 1B | **~−$1,674** class |
| **ATO Annual / CTR** (lodge) | **Tax (ex GST)** | `totalIncomeExGst` | `totalExpensesExGst` | `netProfitExGst` |

Cash reconciliation footnote on Annual card may still show −$927 — **do not paste cash into CTR**.

## Cash-universe root cause (fixed)

Same metrics formula, different post-processing of Cash Expenses:

| Path | Cash Expenses |
|------|----------------|
| **Biz Intel** | Merge into period; **no** OCR collapse on bank+cash |
| **ATO (old)** | `repairStatementDateAnomalies` on combined set collapsed two same-day Stamp zones → kept one |

Guards: skip OCR collapse for `manual` / `cash_*`; `prepareLodgmentTransactions` repairs bank only then reattaches cash; ISO date filter in period-scope.

## Invariant

For the **same FY** and scope `full`:

1. **Transaction set** — Biz Intel and ATO Annual/CTR include the **same** cash + bank P&L rows (both Stamp zones).
2. **ATO copy fields** — Annual totals / CTR Item 6–7 / profit use **`*ExGst`**, not cash totals.
3. **Biz Intel cards** — primary cash; tax secondary (see `accounting-pl-gst-basis.mdc`).

Regression: `lib/ato-lodgment/biz-intel-annual-ctr-cash-parity.test.ts`  
(cash universe vs Biz Intel cash; Annual/CTR field amounts vs `totalExpensesExGst`).

## Do not

- Treat ~$13,012 as “correct FY cash expenses” when Biz Intel shows ~$15,346
- Explain the **$2,334** Stamp-zone gap as GST ÷11
- Paste Biz Intel cash Net (−$927) into company tax return / myTax as taxable profit
- Run OCR date-collapse on a feed that already includes Manual Cash Expenses
